{"parentUuid":"a08607d0-27fb-4ff2-8f63-3762d7f17ee8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NegFq7WFpfV7ZRLKbTmfWz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not quite — let me unpack both parts:\n\n**1. \"Only local branches\":** Neither branch filtering nor `--all-branches` actually enumerates git branches. The filter is against each checkpoint's stored `branch` string, set from `GetCurrentBranchName(repo)` at the moment the checkpoint was condensed (`manual_commit_condensation.go:223`). So whether `main` exists locally or only as `origin/main` in your clone is irrelevant — what matters is which branch was checked out when the commit was made. `--all-branches` just disables the filter entirely; every checkpoint in the time window is included regardless of stored branch.\n\n**2. \"Filters out entire branches\":** There is no explicit `entire/…` filter. But in practice those branches never appear in the output because:\n- `summary.Branch` is captured at condensation time, when the user is on their working branch (`main`, `my-feature`, …), never on a shadow branch `entire/<hash>-<hash>`.\n- Enumeration reads checkpoint metadata from the `entire/checkpoints/v1` orphan branch (`store.ListCommitted`). That ref is the *storage location* — it's not a `summary.Branch` value.\n- The reachability fallback walks `git log` of commits on your working tree, not on `entire/…` refs.\n\nSo the only way `entire/*` could leak into a dispatch is if someone manually checked out a shadow branch and committed — pathological, not a real flow.\n\nIf you want a belt-and-suspenders defensive filter (\"drop any checkpoint whose `summary.Branch` starts with `entire/`\"), I can add it — but it would be protecting against a case that the data model already makes impossible. Want me to add it anyway?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_