{"parentUuid":"1d70c5c2-ee16-4ebe-b3b3-69886edcc26b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HkdimGoyN8Z8SNviy9s9qC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--all-branches` is the \"no branch filter\" switch — it tells dispatch to ignore which branch each checkpoint was made on.\n\n**Local mode** (`mode_local.go:141-162`):\n- `branchSet` stays empty and the whole `if !opts.AllBranches { ... }` filter block is skipped.\n- The reachability fallback isn't even computed — the gate is `opts.ImplicitCurrentBranch && !opts.AllBranches`.\n- Every committed checkpoint in the time window is included, regardless of which branch was checked out when it was condensed.\n\n**Server mode** (`mode_cloud.go` → API):\n- The CLI serializes branches as the string sentinel `\"all\"` in the request body (see `CreateDispatchRequest.MarshalJSON` at `cloud.go:158`).\n- The server's `resolveRepoBranches` (`api/src/lib/dispatch.ts:447`) expands `\"all\"` by querying `db.checkpoints.getBranchesWithCheckpoints(repoId)` — every distinct branch value that has any checkpoint for this repo. It then runs the per-branch checkpoint query for each.\n- Result: every checkpoint across every branch you have checkpoints on, inside the time window.\n\nSame semantic in both modes: **drop the branch filter**. The only scoping left is the `--since/--until` time window (and in server mode, your repo access).\n\nPractical consequence: running `entire dispatch --all-branches` on `my-feature` will include a/b/c from main AND d/e/f from my-feature AND anything from any other feature branch you've touched — the opposite of the branch-scoping we just fixed for the implicit default."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":613,"cache_read_input_tokens":214614,"output_tokens":1058,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache