r entirely.\n\nFocus areas — I want your independent read on each:\n\n1. **Correctness of the default-branch resolution** in `defaultBranchRef` / `branchLocalRevRange` (cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go). Edge cases to consider: detached HEAD, user currently on `main`, `origin/HEAD` not set, `main..HEAD` being empty. Are there cases where the reachability fallback silently returns the wrong set?\n\n2. **Forward-compat decoder change** in cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud.go. Is dropping `DisallowUnknownFields` on the production decoder the right tradeoff? Any risk of silently ignored server fields masking real bugs?\n\n3. **Cloud payload surgery**. `CreateDispatchRequest.MarshalJSON` is gone — does the server still get the fields it needs? Is the 5-repo cap enforced at the right layer? Should it be enforced server-side too?\n\n4. **`--all-branches` local-mode rewrite** in `enumerateRepoCandidates`. The flag went from \"skip branch filter\" to \"filter by local refs\". Is there user-facing behavior change I should warn about? Will checkpoints tagged with branch names that got renamed/rebased get silently dropped?\n\n5. **The `entire/` reserved-prefix filter** in `localBranchNames`. It uses `checkpoint.ShadowBranchPrefix`. Could a user ever legitimately have a branch named `entire/...` that this excludes?\n\n6. **Security**: the cloud client uses `Bearer` auth; any auth handling concerns? Any prompt-injection risk in the voice string / repo names that get forwarded to the server?\n\n7. **Test coverage**: are the tests on this branch genuinely exercising the new behavior, or mostly happy-path smoke tests? Are there edge cases missing?\n\nAlso flag anything else that jumps out — dead code, inconsistent error handling, stale docstrings, missing context propagation, things that changed elsewhere in the diff that shouldn't have.\n\nPlease write for a senior engineer who is going to read this quickly before merging. Tight, skeptical, specific — file:line references for ever