approach).\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 Nit\n\n**12. `branchLocalRevRange` swallows `defaultBranchRef` errors entirely.**\n`mode_local.go:248-254`. No logging on fallback. Users running against a repo with an unusual default branch have no way to know the filter defaulted to `HEAD` — they'll just see \"too many checkpoints.\" A single `logging.Debug` call with the chosen base would help.\n\n**13. `runGitOutput` treats all non-zero exits as \"ref doesn't exist\".**\n`mode_local.go:274-281`. A `.git/index.lock` or permission error looks identical to \"no such ref.\" Not actionable for a nit, but worth a comment.\n\n**14. `findCommitSubjectByCheckpoint` uses `git log --all` which includes `refs/remotes/*`.**\n`mode_local.go:334-345`. On repos with multiple remotes, this may pick up a stale subject from a rewritten commit on another fork. Narrow to `--branches --remotes` or just `HEAD`-reachable? Marginal.\n\n**15. `Options.RepoPaths` does double duty.**\nIn cloud mode the field holds org/repo slugs; in local mode it holds filesystem paths. Today `ResolveOptions` rejects `--repos` + `--local`, so the two never mix, but the field name implies filesystem. Rename to `Repos` or split into `RepoSlugs`/`RepoFSPaths`.\n\n**16. `firstAt` / `lastAt` asymmetry.**\n`mode_local.go:409-430`. `firstAt` skips zero-valued `CreatedAt`, `lastAt` doesn't (`time.Time{}.After(time.Time{})` is false, so it's still correct — but a future reader has to prove that). Either skip in both or neither, for symmetry.\n\n**17. Test names overclaim in subtle ways.**\n`TestLocalMode_AllBranchesRestrictsToLocalBranches` (line 480) asserts the \"should not appear\" bullet is absent but doesn't positively assert the feature-a checkpoint IS present. If `seedCommittedCheckpoint` quietly broke, the test would still pass.\n\n**18. `--repos` flag help says \"cloud repo slugs.\"**\n`dispatch.go:74`. Clear for the cloud case. But since `--repos` is rejected with `--local`, maybe worth saying \"cloud mode only\" explicitly to save a support ticket.\n\n**19. No test for `--org` flag removal.**\nA test of the form `TestDispatchCmd_OrgFlagIsNotRegistered` that calls `cmd.Flags().Lookup(\"org\")` and asserts nil would prevent accidental re-addition. Maybe overkill.\n\n---\n\n## Things verified / done well\n\n- **Prompt-injection posture is solid.** The local-mode generation prompt at `generate.go:47-68` explicitly names repo names, branch names, commit messages, bullets, warnings, and voice preference as untrusted and tells the model not to follow them. The `<dispatch_data>`/`<voice_preference>` tags are escaped case-insensitively (`dispatchPromptTagPattern` at `generate.go:105`), and the voice string is additionally stripped of control chars + BiDi overrides + zero-width chars (`generate.go:194-207`). This is above the norm.\n- **Bearer-token handling is clean.** Token is only read via `auth.LookupCurrentToken`, only sent to the configured base URL, never logged. No obvious exfil path. The `StatusUnauthorized` branch returns a user-friendly error without echoing the token.\n- **Forward-compat decoder change is the right call.** Strictness on clients + a rolling server = guaranteed CLI break whenever the server adds a field. The tradeoff (silently-ignored response fields) is strictly better than the old tradeoff (silent 100% failure). The risk of masking real server-side bugs is low because the fields in question (warnings, totals) are cosmetic, and the CLI still validates presence of what it uses (`dispatch.GeneratedText` at `mode_cloud.go:73-75`).\n- **Parallelism in `runLocal` is textbook `errgroup` usage.** `groupCtx` is threaded through, mutex-guarded slice append, `group.Wait()` before consuming. Clean.\n- **`localBranchNames` correctly excludes the `entire/` reserved prefix.** `mode_local.go:312-332` + `checkpoint/temporary.go:34-35`. It is not a legitimate concern for a user-named branch: the checkpoint strategy uses `entire/` aggressively for shadow branches and `entire/checkpoints/v1` — collisions would already break checkpointing regardless of dispatch. Safe to filter.\n- **Custom `MarshalJSON` removal is clean.** No partial states left behind; payload-shape test (`cloud_test.go:69-101`) asserts the right negatives.\n- **`ResolveOptions` validation ordering is right.** Rejects `--repos + --local` before checking cap, so you don't get a confusing \"at most 5 repos\" error when the real problem is mode conflict.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES** — the default-branch resolution (#1) is a real silent-wrong-answer bug on a non-`main`/`master` default, and the test fragility (#3) hides it. Those two plus the server-side cap (#2) need addressing. Everything else is should-fix or nit and can be rolled into a follow-up. Once #1–#3 are in I'd approve.\n\nEstimated effort: **~2–3 hours** for #1 (add `git config` + `remote show` probe, new test), **30 min** for #2 (server-side enforcement is separate, but add the client-side defense-in-depth in `runServer`), **15 min** for #3 (make shim append).\n\n---\n\nFiles referenced:\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local_test.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud_test.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud_test.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go`\n- `/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go`\n- `