{"parentUuid":"0542efb4-dc5e-4d42-bb9f-99f9807ef4c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XRwyQD48BhG6CFmK64ArqT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests green, only the pre-existing goconst warning remains. Both fixes are in place.\n\n---\n\n## Explanation of the stale `origin/HEAD` finding (not fixed)\n\nCodex is right that this is still a hole; I'll explain the mechanism and the fix shape so you can decide when to close it.\n\n**The hole in `defaultBranchRef` (`mode_local.go:259-272`):**\n\n```go\nfunc defaultBranchRef(ctx context.Context, repoRoot string) string {\n    if out, ok := runGitOutput(ctx, repoRoot, \"symbolic-ref\", \"--quiet\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"); ok {\n        ref := strings.TrimSpace(out)\n        if strings.HasPrefix(ref, \"refs/remotes/\") {\n            return strings.TrimPrefix(ref, \"refs/remotes/\")   // ← returns unchecked\n        }\n    }\n    for _, candidate := range []string{\"origin/main\", \"origin/master\", \"main\", \"master\"} {\n        if _, ok := runGitOutput(ctx, repoRoot, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"--quiet\", candidate); !ok {\n            continue\n        }\n        if _, ok := runGitOutput(ctx, repoRoot, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", candidate, \"HEAD\"); ok {\n            return candidate   // ← ancestor check applied here\n        }\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\n\nThe `merge-base --is-ancestor` ancestor check only runs in the *fallback* loop. The `origin/HEAD` fast-path returns whatever symbolic-ref says without verifying the target is an ancestor of HEAD. Two realistic ways this goes wrong:\n\n1. **Default-branch rename.** Repo renamed `master` → `main`. `git clone` from years ago set `origin/HEAD -> refs/remotes/origin/master`. No-one ran `git remote set-head origin -a` since. The ref still resolves; `master` now points wherever it last was (possibly stale or diverged). `branchLocalRevRange` returns `origin/master..HEAD`, and \"feature work\" in a dispatch includes every commit on the new `main` that was made since the rename.\n\n2. **Remote config drift.** Someone manually set `git remote set-head origin <old-branch>` for local convenience, or a tool did. `origin/HEAD` now points at a ref that isn't the real default branch. Same leak.\n\nIn both cases, `git log origin/master..HEAD` silently produces the wrong set, and the symptom the fix was supposed to prevent (pre-branch history leaking into a feature-branch dispatch) comes back — but harder to notice because `origin/HEAD` *feels* authoritative.\n\n**The fix shape when you're ready:**\n\nApply the same `merge-base --is-ancestor` guard to the `origin/HEAD` path:\n\n```go\nif out, ok := runGitOutput(ctx, repoRoot, \"symbolic-ref\", \"--quiet\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"); ok {\n    ref := strings.TrimSpace(out)\n    if strings.HasPrefix(ref, \"refs/remotes/\") {\n        candidate := strings.TrimPrefix(ref, \"refs/remotes/\")\n        if _, ok := runGitOutput(ctx, repoRoot, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", candidate, \"HEAD\"); ok {\n            return candidate\n        }\n    }\n}\n// fallback loop unchanged\n```\n\nPlus a regression test: init a repo, set `origin/HEAD` to a ref on a disjoint history (or force-update it), and assert `defaultBranchRef` returns `\"\"`. The existing `TestDefaultBranchRef_RejectsStaleRefNotAncestorOfHEAD` is the template — it does exactly this for the fallback path, just needs a sibling that exercises the symbolic-ref branch.\n\nWant me to commit the HTTPS-guard fix + `-h` visibility now? Happy to do the stale-`origin/HEAD` fix in a follow-up commit if you'd like, or fold it in."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":413969,"output_tokens":1385,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":606,