{"parentUuid":"2f6dc985-a1f5-4e1a-a727-3dcc4acf7f75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MdQNstb5RkwPTQQZpU9bey","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AkdXg8XsDR2qPvLYeS4tUb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/alisha/.claude/plans/projects-wt-cli-entire-dispatch-codex-e-floofy-music.md","content":"# Plan: add `--insecure-http-auth` flag to `entire dispatch`\n\n## Context\n\nThe cloud dispatch path now enforces `api.RequireSecureURL` on the base URL\nbefore sending a bearer token (committed as `51b0f8cd6`). That gate fires the\nstandard `api.ErrInsecureHTTP` error, which is worded as:\n\n> refusing to use insecure http:// base URL for authentication (use --insecure-http-auth to override)\n\nBut `entire dispatch` never registered the `--insecure-http-auth` flag, so the\nerror text is a lie for this subcommand — running `entire dispatch\n--insecure-http-auth` just falls through to cobra's usage help because the flag\nis unknown. Other authenticated commands (`login`, `trail`) do register it as a\nhidden local-dev override. `dispatch` should follow the same convention so\nlocal-dev users can point it at `http://localhost:8787` and the error message\nstops making promises it can't keep.\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror `login.go` (single-command, local flag). Do not reach for a persistent\nflag on the root command — there is no subcommand tree here, and adding a root-\nlevel flag would leak insecure-HTTP semantics onto every command.\n\nThread the flag through the existing `dispatch.Options` → `ResolveOptions` →\n`runServer` path, gate `requireSecureDispatchURL` on it, and keep the test-\nswappable hook (`requireSecureDispatchURL`) as-is so existing cloud tests keep\nworking.\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go` — add `flagInsecureHTTPAuth` local var + hidden\n  flag registration; pass it through `parseDispatchFlags` →\n  `resolveDispatchOptions`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/dispatch.go` — add `InsecureHTTPAuth bool` to\n  `Options`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go` — add `flagInsecureHTTPAuth` parameter\n  to `ResolveOptions` and forward it into the returned `Options`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go` — skip the\n  `requireSecureDispatchURL` call when `opts.InsecureHTTPAuth` is true.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go` — wizard always passes `false` (no UI\n  exposure); update the two `resolveDispatchOptions` callers so the new\n  parameter compiles.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_test.go` — add a unit test asserting the flag\n  propagates into `Options.InsecureHTTPAuth`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options_test.go` — add a unit test asserting the\n  new parameter is forwarded; update the existing calls to pass `false`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud_test.go` — add a regression test\n  `TestServerMode_InsecureHTTPAuthBypassesSecureURLCheck` that runs dispatch\n  against an `http://` `httptest.NewServer`, sets\n  `Options{InsecureHTTPAuth: true}`, and confirms the HTTPS guard is skipped.\n  Do **not** stub `requireSecureDispatchURL` — the whole point is exercising\n  the real gate.\n\nThe existing security regression test `TestServerMode_RejectsPlainHTTPBaseURL`\nalready covers the `InsecureHTTPAuth == false` path and should stay unchanged.\n\n## Reused utilities\n\n- `api.RequireSecureURL` (`cmd/entire/cli/api/base_url.go:59`) — unchanged.\n- `api.ErrInsecureHTTP` error sentinel — unchanged; the error's suggestion\n  text finally becomes actionable once the flag exists.\n- Flag convention: `cmd.Flags().BoolVar` + `cmd.Flags().MarkHidden` as in\n  `login.go:56-59`.\n- Package-level `requireSecureDispatchURL` test hook in `mode_cloud.go` —\n  keep; tests that need to bypass without exercising the flag still use\n  `stubCloudDispatchAuth(t)`.\n\n## Sketch of the key diffs\n\n`dispatch/dispatch.go`:\n```go\ntype Options struct {\n    Mode                  Mode\n    RepoPaths             []string\n    Since                 string\n    Until                 string\n    Branches              []string\n    AllBranches           bool\n    ImplicitCurrentBranch bool\n    Voice                 string\n    InsecureHTTPAuth      bool   // new\n}\n```\n\n`dispatch/mode_cloud.go`:\n```go\nbaseURL := api.BaseURL()\nif !opts.InsecureHTTPAuth {\n    if err := requireSecureDispatchURL(baseURL); err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"dispatch base URL: %w\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`dispatch.go`:\n```go\nvar flagInsecureHTTPAuth bool\n// ...\ncmd.Flags().BoolVar(&flagInsecureHTTPAuth, \"insecure-http-auth\", false,\n    \"Allow authentication over plain HTTP (insecure, for local development only)\")\nif err := cmd.Flags().MarkHidden(\"insecure-http-auth\"); err != nil {\n    panic(fmt.Sprintf(\"hide insecure-http-auth flag: %v\", err))\n}\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — only the pre-existing `generate_test.go`\n   goconst warning should remain.\n2. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -run Dispatch` — all existing dispatch tests\n   plus the two new ones pass.\n3. Build: `go build -o /tmp/entire ./cmd/entire`.\n4. End-to-end smoke:\n   - `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 /tmp/entire dispatch` →\n     still rejected with `ErrInsecureHTTP` (existing behaviour).\n   - `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787 /tmp/entire dispatch\n     --insecure-http-auth` → proceeds past the HTTPS gate and attempts the\n     actual request (will fail only on connection / auth, not on scheme\n     validation). This is the behaviour the user just tried and saw fail.\n5. `/tmp/entire dispatch -h` → `--insecure-http-auth` is absent (hidden), but\n   help still lists the other flags.\n6. `/tmp/entire dispatch --help | grep insecure` → empty (flag is hidden).\n7. `/tmp/entire -h` → `dispatch` still listed (unchanged from the previous\n   commit that unhid it).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any behaviour change when `--insecure-http-auth` is not passed.\n- Plumbing the flag through the dispatch wizard UI. Wizard is cloud-\n  default-ish and users running it are not doing local-HTTP development.\n- Changing `api.ErrInsecureHTTP` wording.\n- Anything on the server-side / API repo.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3924,"cache_read_input_tokens":422125,"output_tokens":3209,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3209,"cache_read_input_tokens":422125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3924},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaMUoNycMBB8UJmwts2vq","type":"assistant","uuid":"00bd289a-a341-48cd-8692-135051bdefdf","timestamp":"2026-04-23T22:20:17.949Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/Projects/wt/cli/entire-dispatch-codex","sessionId":"257590f6-9a50-435b-8fa5-1d93575cabf5","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"entire-dispatch-codex","slug":"projects-wt-cli-entire-dispatch-codex-e-floofy-music"}
